+## Migration 0008: retained dispatch observation
+
+`0008_dispatch_observation.sql` adds an immutable dispatch-time record in the
+existing authority database. The `Held -> DispatchAttempted` transition records
+it atomically; its insertion participates in the same dirty frontier and change
+journal. Timeout, expiry, restart and terminal archival never move or delete
+that instant. Settlement can therefore accept still-valid signed evidence
+observed after dispatch but delivered after a later lifecycle update, while
+continuing to reject evidence observed before dispatch.
+
+The table starts empty on upgrade. Old rows without a retained dispatch instant
+continue to use their existing `updated_at_ms` as a conservative lower bound.
+No historical time is invented or lowered. Such an old indeterminate operation
+may require a new, independently authenticated terminal observation; the
+upgrade alone cannot release its quota. The legacy full-state seed is unchanged
+when the new table is empty. Nonempty unseeded stores include these records in
+the snapshot, while seeded stores fold the new journal domain.
+
+This is a coordinated storage upgrade and a downgrade boundary. Deploy only
+with matching binary, migration and checkpoint qualification. An old binary
+must not reopen the new schema. The dispatch record shares the reservation's
+immutable retention obligation and remains present after terminal archival.
+
 ## Binary/store matrix
 
 | Binary | Store | Result |
 | --- | --- | --- |
-| current | predecessor through 0005 | migrate through 0007, seed legacy root at first frontier evaluation, verify, open |
-| current | current 0006/0007 | verify accumulator/journal/guards/schema, open |
+| current | predecessor through 0005 | migrate through 0008, seed legacy root at first frontier evaluation, verify, open |
+| current | predecessor 0006/0007 | add empty dispatch-observation table, verify accumulator/journal/guards/schema, open |
+| current | current 0008 | verify dispatch-observation and frontier guards, open |
 | current | newer unknown | fail closed |
-| predecessor | current 0006/0007 | unsupported; restore a matched pre-0006 pair |
+| predecessor | current 0008 | unsupported; restore only an independently approved matched backup pair |
